From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Kuhn <martin@kuhn.host>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] u-boot: load EFI binaries above fdt_addr_r, pick the D0 DT on
 D0 boards

0002: rpi.env had kernel_addr_r=0x00080000 and fdt_addr_r=0x02600000.
The EFI network boot TFTPs the ~160M Talos UKI to kernel_addr_r and then
the DT to fdt_addr_r, i.e. into the UKI's initrd: the initramfs fails its
zstd checksum and Talos dies with "failed to mount squashfs: openfs
failed: failed to create root filesystem: FSCONFIG_CMD_CREATE failed:
invalid argument". Move kernel_addr_r to 0x02800000 and ramdisk_addr_r
to 0x1a800000. Reproduced and verified in QEMU (U-Boot EFI net boot of
the v1.14.1 UKI: corrupt with the old address, boots with the new).

0003: fdtfile is broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb for both Pi 5 steppings;
select broadcom/bcm2712-d-rpi-5-b.dtb when the firmware DT has the D0
pin controller ("brcm,bcm2712d0-pinctrl").
---
 ...load-the-kernel-UKI-above-fdt_addr_r.patch | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 ...ine-D0-device-tree-on-Pi-5-D0-boards.patch | 31 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 68 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 artifacts/u-boot/patches/0002-rpi-load-the-kernel-UKI-above-fdt_addr_r.patch
 create mode 100644 artifacts/u-boot/patches/0003-rpi-pick-the-mainline-D0-device-tree-on-Pi-5-D0-boards.patch

diff --git a/artifacts/u-boot/patches/0002-rpi-load-the-kernel-UKI-above-fdt_addr_r.patch b/artifacts/u-boot/patches/0002-rpi-load-the-kernel-UKI-above-fdt_addr_r.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a668672
--- /dev/null
+++ b/artifacts/u-boot/patches/0002-rpi-load-the-kernel-UKI-above-fdt_addr_r.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+From: Martin Kuhn <martin@kuhn.host>
+Subject: [PATCH] rpi: load the kernel/UKI above fdt_addr_r
+
+The EFI network boot (boot/bootmeth_efi.c) TFTPs the EFI binary to
+kernel_addr_r and afterwards the device tree to fdt_addr_r. With
+kernel_addr_r=0x00080000 and fdt_addr_r=0x02600000 any EFI binary larger
+than 37.5M is overwritten by the DT. The Talos UKI is ~160M: the DT lands
+in its initrd, the initramfs fails its zstd checksum ("rootfs image is not
+initramfs (ZSTD-compressed data is corrupt)") and Talos cannot mount its
+squashfs rootfs.
+
+Move kernel_addr_r to 0x02800000 (2M aligned, after the 1M script, pxefile
+and fdt slots) and ramdisk_addr_r to 0x1a800000, a 384M window.
+---
+--- a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env
++++ b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.env
+@@ -68,10 +68,18 @@
+ fdt_high=ffffffff
+ initrd_high=ffffffff
+ #endif
+-kernel_addr_r=0x00080000
++/*
++ * Talos: the kernel slot goes above the small buffers. The EFI network boot
++ * (bootmeth_efi) TFTPs the whole UKI (~160M) to kernel_addr_r and then the
++ * device tree to fdt_addr_r; with kernel_addr_r=0x00080000 the DT landed
++ * inside the UKI's initrd and corrupted it. 0x02800000 is 2M aligned (booti
++ * needs no relocation) and leaves 384M for the kernel/UKI before
++ * ramdisk_addr_r, which still fits a 1G board.
++ */
+ scriptaddr=0x02400000
+ pxefile_addr_r=0x02500000
+ fdt_addr_r=0x02600000
+-ramdisk_addr_r=0x02700000
++kernel_addr_r=0x02800000
++ramdisk_addr_r=0x1a800000
+ 
+ boot_targets=mmc usb pxe dhcp
diff --git a/artifacts/u-boot/patches/0003-rpi-pick-the-mainline-D0-device-tree-on-Pi-5-D0-boards.patch b/artifacts/u-boot/patches/0003-rpi-pick-the-mainline-D0-device-tree-on-Pi-5-D0-boards.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c1dd64d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/artifacts/u-boot/patches/0003-rpi-pick-the-mainline-D0-device-tree-on-Pi-5-D0-boards.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+From: Martin Kuhn <martin@kuhn.host>
+Subject: [PATCH] rpi: pick the mainline D0 device tree on Pi 5 D0 boards
+
+The Pi 5 Model B revision code (0x17) is the same for the C1 and D0 SoC
+steppings, so fdtfile is always broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb. Mainline
+Linux has a separate DT for D0 (bcm2712-d-rpi-5-b.dtb). The firmware
+passes its D0 DT (bcm2712d0-rpi-5-b.dtb) on D0 boards, which is the only
+one with a "brcm,bcm2712d0-pinctrl" node; use that to select the D0 file.
+---
+--- a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
++++ b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
+@@ -351,6 +351,19 @@
+ 		return;
+ 
+ 	fdtfile = model->fdtfile;
++
++	/*
++	 * Talos: the Pi 5 Model B revision code is the same for the C1 and D0
++	 * SoC steppings, but mainline Linux has a separate DT for D0. The
++	 * firmware hands over its D0 DT (bcm2712d0-rpi-5-b.dtb) on D0 boards,
++	 * recognisable by its D0 pin controller.
++	 */
++	if (!strcmp(fdtfile, DTB_DIR "bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb") &&
++	    fdt_magic(fw_dtb_pointer) == FDT_MAGIC &&
++	    fdt_node_offset_by_compatible((void *)fw_dtb_pointer, -1,
++					  "brcm,bcm2712d0-pinctrl") >= 0)
++		fdtfile = DTB_DIR "bcm2712-d-rpi-5-b.dtb";
++
+ 	env_set("fdtfile", fdtfile);
+ }
+ 
